Claim type: bounded_theorem

On a supplied strong spectral domain, a finite static nearest-neighbor qubit bus can implement the stated old-plant rotation over a finite observation window while keeping all controller outputs and bounding every added incident interaction load by one accuracy-independent constant. Arbitrarily long runtime and demanding precision remain possible. The complete literal old Hamiltonian stays installed. This is conditional mathematics with supplied preparation, phase references and isolation; it is not a generic compiler theorem or native controller realization.

The exact author proof and exposed review follow once each, unchanged. Source acceptance is `cc2e519d8c4de174cc98137a8f9c5e2ae7df6a782adfd93d7389d1eac346c726`, recorded 2026-10-16T01:15:02.830146+00:00; controlling qualifications are `a182e0074ac9b8ed1d9e9e57627d289754252e2969446099ed502e229bf61880`. The 2026-10-15 name is the campaign date. Source acceptance does not accept this new wrapper, final canonical integration, publication or retained status. Historical pending-review sentences remain original source text.

## 1. Conditional theorem and exact scope

Fix the entire finite old qubit plant, including original apparatus, memory and filler factors, with computable onsite/ordinary-nearest-neighbor Hermitian H. Every literal old term has coefficient one in its physical units. Supply h>=||H||, time unit t_*>0, observation window w>=0, and W=exp(i theta0)exp(-iL), L=L*. The whole old input can be arbitrary and correlated with a passive reference.

Additional supplied hypotheses are simple complete energies E_0<...<E_(d-1), d>=2; distinct positive pair gaps; and a designated local dimensionless Hermitian B on an accessible old qubit p whose energy-basis B_ab is nonzero for every a!=b. A consistent computable spectral decomposition, or sufficient strict isolation data, is supplied. These hypotheses are not derived from the earlier augmented Lie certificate. No perturbation of H is used to impose them.

The geometry also has content: p can be placed at (0,0,0), the old occupied sites lie in a finite nonnegative-coordinate box, and the displayed exterior corridors are empty, or an explicitly supplied vacant embedding of the same tree is available. Existing sites are not moved or reinitialized. Unlisted couplings must be isolated or included in a complete-generator error budget. One accessible neighbor alone does not establish these vacant corridors.

For a fixed exact L with its needed support/phase data supplied, the accepted construction gives, for every 0<epsilon<=1, finite controller size, static positive added blocks, T>0 and a supplied pure controller state. At every t=T+s, 0<=s<=w, its complete output is within epsilon in unhalved trace norm of the isometry

```
exp[-i chi(t)] |0_bus>
  tensor [tensor_l exp(-it omega_l N_l)|Alpha_l(phi_l)>]
  tensor [exp(-isH) W exp(-iTH)],
chi(t)=R(xi)t+c_old xi^2 t+theta0,       T=t_*/xi^2.
```

The last factor acts on the entire old input and is tensored with reference identity. Both literal old-time flows, every bus/source factor and the actual reserve phase remain. The theorem is a finite observation-window assertion; it does not provide permanent halt, autonomous readout, reusable apparatus or a physical energy interpretation.

The author exact-L statement is qualified: a bare oracle for arbitrary computable entries does not decide exact zero/support or choose a unit phase discontinuously at zero. Section 5 below gives the separately attributed effective approximate-target repair. These are distinct assertions.

## 2. Finite construction and full-space gap

Set k=d-1, m=2k and q=d(d-1)/2. There is one length-N source per positive old gap omega_l=E_a-E_b, N>=2. The bus has b=m+4q qubits, independent of epsilon for fixed plant. The full addition has b+qN sites and b+qN added edges, counting the single old/new port edge.

The diagonal calibration uses

```
f_a(mu)=sum_b |B_ba|^2/(E_a-E_b-mu),
F(mu)=(f_a(mu)-f_0(mu))_(a>0),
y=(L_aa-L_00)_(a>0)/t_*.
```

Near Delta_a=E_a-E_0, distinct gaps give only the a-th pole, with opposite residues at Delta_a±delta. Scaling the 2k columns by delta/|B_0a|^2 gives matrices V_+→I, V_-→-I. For sufficiently small delta, `M=-V_+^-1 V_-` has M1>1/2 entrywise. The positive null vector `(D_delta M1,D_delta 1)` lets one add a sufficiently large finite multiple to `(F_+^-1 y,0)` to obtain strictly positive weights. Fixed small energy boxes preserve these strict conditions. An arbitrary first offset need not work; the historical failed trials remain evidence of that limitation.

The positive weights determine a Jacobi core with specified energies mu_j and root spectral weights p_j=w_j/S, S=sum w_j. The physical port strength is v_p=sqrt(S); it varies during calibration. The open core is placed along negative x, followed by a backbone of 3q sites, one routing leaf per gap, and source rays in negative z separated by three in x. Router hopping is a small positive rho and router field nu lies above all core energies and positive gaps. New-site degree is at most three.

For each source,

```
N_l=sum_j n_(l,j),
L_l=J_F sum_j(I-SWAP_(l,j;l,j+1)),
H_l=omega_l N_l+L_l,
K0=H+H_bus+sum_l H_l,
K0 J_code=J_code F_code,      F_code=H+sum_l omega_l N_l.
```

The code consists of bus vacuum and each complete symmetric source subspace. The positive swap sum has exactly that symmetric kernel and commutes with source SU(2). All excitation sectors are present in the physical finite matrices.

At rho=0 only the open Jacobi core is transformed to free fermions; its full spectrum is formed from subsets of fixed mu_j, independent of positive weights. Isolated router sites and source sectors add their own energies. A Q/P difference has form

```
sum_(j in S) mu_j+r nu+J_F a+(E_b-E_c)+sum_l omega_l z_l,
```

where a>=0 and a Q state forces at least one nonzero coefficient among the free mu_j,nu,J_F. At each finite N, finitely many proper hyperplanes cannot fill the open parameter box. Dovetailed rational parameter choices with certified strict spectral enclosures find a positive complete separation delta_0 without an equality oracle or a favorable search bound. Internal code degeneracies are retained.

At nonzero routing the complete many-qubit perturbation has norm <=4q rho. The code remains unchanged, so full separation stays at least delta_0-4q rho. This survives the later weight adjustment because the zero-route spectrum is weight-independent. A branched XY bus is not asserted to have one-particle subset-sum spectrum.

The router Schur correction at every old difference is rank one with norm e=rho^2/Delta_R. The exact finite derivative bounds in the author proof make the calibration map a contraction after rho is chosen small enough for its gap, resolvent and derivative inequalities. Thus a computable positive calibrated weight vector exists, with actual port factor sqrt(S). The proof pays all Gram-determinant denominators and preserves the full gap. Unique-path cofactor expansion then makes every root-to-leaf response G_l nonzero: each path traverses the whole core, its off-path components are high-energy router subtrees, and all path hoppings are positive. This is a specific tree argument, not a generic assertion about interior Jacobi inverse entries.

## 3. Complete source correction and retained fluctuation

For a symmetric source vector |k>, let chi_k=Q_s sigma_-^1|k>. Its squared norm is k(k-1)/N^2. The additional ladder identity

```
S_- chi_k=sqrt[k(N-k+1)] chi_(k-1),      S_+ chi_N=0
```

places all nonzero chi_k in the same spin-(N/2-1) highest-weight multiplicity ladder. Since the source resolvent commutes with SU(2), its normalized ladder contraction is one b_N(c). Therefore, on the entire symmetric code,

```
P_s sigma_+^1(L_l+c)^-1 sigma_-^1 P_s
 = k(N-k+1)/(N^2 c)+b_N(c)k(k-1)/N^2.
```

The complete Q/P gap proves the needed full source inverse exists for c=lambda_j-omega_l; the one-hole calculation of b_N is only a convenience. Norm identities alone would not establish this lemma.

With `V=v_p B_p X_c1+sum_l r_l(T_(u_l,a_l1))`, PVP=0. Two actions from and back to bus vacuum give: calibrated old diagonal entries `d_a=L_aa/t_*+c_old`; same-source self-energy `A_l k/N+(B_l-A_l)k(k-1)/N^2`; and the unique mixed resonant coefficient

```
kappa_ab=-v_p r_l B_ab G_l,
r_l=2|L_ab|/(t_* v_p |B_ab G_l|).
```

There is no factor two. Distinct-source transfers are nonresonant. Longer-sum code degeneracies add no new connected two-action terms. The full source counterterms

```
A2=sum_l[u_l sum_j n_(l,j)+v_l sum_j n_(l,j)n_(l,j+1)],
u_l=-A_l/N,            v_l=-(B_l-A_l)/N
```

cancel the whole self-energy on code. Their off-code action is retained in the complete corrector. The secular generator is

```
D=c_old I+sum_a L_aa|a><a|/t_*
   +sum_(a>b)[kappa_ab |a><b| S_(l,-)/N+h.c.],
[D,F_code]=0.
```

On supplied coherent product sources Alpha_l(phi)=[(|0>+exp(i phi)|1>)/sqrt(2)]^tensor N, the distinct one-beta residuals are orthogonal. The full retained-output norm is `B_L/sqrt(N)`, where `B_L=t_*^-1 max_a sqrt(sum_(b!=a)|L_ab|^2)`. Small routed responses cancel from this fluctuation constant; their cost remains in physical coefficients, corrector bounds and runtime.

The complete finite corrector uses the separated Q/P Sylvester inverse for Z1 and Z2, and only the classified connected old/gap differences for nonzero P/P divisors. Unknown longer code-energy coincidences require no division. For `Z=J_code+xi Z1+xi^2 Z2`,

```
(K0+xi V+xi^2 A2)Z-Z(F_code+xi^2 D)=xi^3 R3+xi^4 R4,
R3=VZ2+A2Z1-Z1D,       R4=A2Z2-Z2D.
```

Bare-code endpoint terms and Duhamel give complete isometry error <=xi C_corr through T+w. The finite, potentially huge C_corr includes every off-code counterterm action. No dressed physical input is substituted. Source fluctuation adds at most `(t_*+w)B_L/sqrt(N)` and the observation window adds `xi^2 w||L||/t_*`.

After T is selected, nonzero target entries use the phase with +omega_l T, equivalently the unit ratio in section 5. It produces `G_phi=exp(iHT)L exp(-iHT)/t_*` and exactly

```
exp(-itH)exp(-i xi^2 t G_phi)
 =exp(-isH)exp[-i(1+xi^2 s/t_*)L]exp(-iTH).
```

Phase choices do not change the Hamiltonian, gap, corrector or load bounds.

## 4. Actual positive blocks, incident cap and resource order

The literal generator is

```
K=K0+xi V+xi^2 A2+R(xi)I,
R(xi)=R_s+R_bus+xi R_V+xi^2 R_A2,
R_s>=h,          R_bus=sum_bus_edges |t_e|,
R_V=v_p||B||+sum_l r_l,
R_A2=sum_l[N max(0,-u_l)+(N-1)max(0,-v_l)].
```

Every reserve is actually installed and its actual value appears in chi(t). A positive exchange block has norm 2|t_e|, a source ferromagnetic block 2J_F, the port block at most 2xi v_p||B||, and reserved onsite/pair counterterms xi^2|u_l| and xi^2|v_l|. H+R_s I is positive as a whole; separate positivity of each old term is not required. No -H term or old-unit rescaling is introduced.

The normalized trace is a different ledger:

```
s_K=s_H+R_s+Tr(B_bus)/2+R_bus
 +sum_l[N omega_l/2+J_F(N-1)/2]+xi R_V
 +xi^2 sum_l[N u_l/2+(N-1)v_l/4
                  +N max(0,-u_l)+(N-1)max(0,-v_l)].
```

No onsite, swap identity part or phase-bearing source factor is deleted. For one fixed bound M_E on base coefficient boxes, bus base incident norm is <=7M_E, source base <=5M_E. With

```
J0=R_s+7M_E,     J1=J2=1/t_*,
ell_V=2(v_p||B||+sum_l r_l),
ell_2=max_l(|u_l|+2|v_l|),
xi ell_V<=J1,      xi^2 ell_2<=J2,
J_*=R_s+7M_E+2/t_*,
```

every added incident load is bounded independently of epsilon. Total reserve, global norm, source size, runtime and precision are not bounded by that assertion. Tiny Green responses and small full gaps may force very small xi.

Choose a positive computable majorant B>=B_L and w_bar>=w. First choose an integer N>=max(2,[8(t_*+w_bar)B/epsilon]^2), using a certified rational upper enclosure and its ceiling with bounded additive excess. Next choose separated spectral data, rho and the calibrated weights, compute responses/source counterterms, and obtain finite corrector/load bounds. Then choose positive xi no larger than

```
min{1, epsilon/[8(C_corr+1)],
 sqrt[epsilon t_*/(8(t_*+w_bar)(1+||L||))],
 J1/(ell_V+J1), sqrt[J2/(ell_2+J2)]}.
```

Finally set T=t_*/xi^2 and source phases. Strict rational selection avoids boundary equality tests. Three isometry allowances <=epsilon/8 give full trace error <=3epsilon/4. Supplied initial trace error <=epsilon/8 relative to the product with its exact unconditional old/reference marginal, and complete self-adjoint generator perturbation with `integral_0^(T+w)||E(t)||dt<=epsilon/16`, give final epsilon. A pointwise physical incident cap needs actual incident budgets or fixed slack as well; an integral error budget alone cannot establish it. Release-time uncertainty needs a paid norm-times-time allocation. None of these suppliers is derived.

## 5. Exact-target qualification and attributed effective repair

For a fixed exact L, existence can use specified support and phases. It is not accepted that arbitrary computable L automatically permits exact zero/support decisions or arg(L_ab). The unit phase z/|z| has no continuous extension at zero. The following separate repair was proposed by root, explicitly checked in the exposed review section 6, and accepted in FINAL_QUALIFICATIONS; it is not silently inserted into the author's unchanged body.

Approximate L in the supplied old-energy basis by rational Hermitian M with `||M-L||<=epsilon/32`. Entry accuracy epsilon/(32d), with Hermitian symmetrization, suffices. The support of M is decidable. For M_ab=0 set r_l=0 and phase one. For nonzero M_ab use

```
exp(i phi_l)=(M_ab/|M_ab|)(conj(kappa_ab)/|kappa_ab|)exp(i omega_l T).
```

Run the entire construction for M at tolerance epsilon/2, including preparation <=epsilon/16 and integrated generator error <=epsilon/32. It gives full trace allowance epsilon/2. Hermitian Duhamel adds at most `2||M-L||<=epsilon/16`, hence total <=9epsilon/16. This comparison retains the same complete source vector and physical old-time flows at the construction's actual T. The spectral coefficient boxes and M_E depend on fixed H,B,t_* rather than M; target-dependent weights, port/source loads and counterterms are absorbed in the later xi-smallness. The common cap therefore survives the rational-target approximation. There is still no favorable runtime, coefficient precision, global norm, search complexity or native realization theorem.

